{
  "kernel": "tp-ising-v1-confirmatory",
  "description": "ising-ews-v1's confirmatory dataset: the 75 runs `ews score` selects (ews.ising.select), 25 per size at L = 16, 32 and 64: on each of seeds 6-10 at 64 replicas, a slow ramp (x = 0.02, eps_L 12 to -8), a staircase and null runs at eps_L 2, 4 and 6. Note 13's 90 counted 15 fast ramps at x = 2, which fill no slot of v1. The tau_c record comes from tp-tauc-l64-l128 and the three dwell files from tp-ising-job-a, as those kernels wrote them, each pinned by sha256. The wheel dataset holds the one wheel built from a clean clone of the tag prereg/ising-ews-v1 and its COMMIT.txt, and `commit` refuses any other. Expected: 6-7.5 T4-hours, 3-4 quota hours and about 12 GB in one session, at most 16.5 GB, under the 18 GB where the runner stops. Never delete or re-make a finished run. A plateau or null block that misses its thermalised check leaves its run complete and its queue running: STATUS lists the run under `thermalised missed`, and the scorer drops that plateau or block and counts it. The first push is the line below without --resume, into a folder of its own. If out/STATUS says incomplete, or the session died, wait until it has stopped and run this one line from the main checkout, which reuses every finished run and continues the unfinished ones: uv run --no-sync python notebooks/kaggle_ising_runs.py --write-kernel notebooks/plans/v1-confirmatory.json ../.wf/kaggle/kernel-v1-confirmatory-resume --resume; kaggle kernels push -p ../.wf/kaggle/kernel-v1-confirmatory-resume",
